<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>The Perth Hills &amp; Eastern Suburbs cover three councils: the City of Swan, the City of Kalamunda and the Shire of Mundaring. Most of Perth sits on sand, but this side of the metro area is different. The Guildford Formation clay outcrops over much of the eastern region, and the foothills below the Darling Scarp are colluvial slopes. Clay moves with moisture in a way sand doesn't, which is why footing and cracking questions come up here more than anywhere else in Perth.</p><p>Kings Park Structural Co is a referral service, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to an independent structural engineer, who quotes you and contracts with you directly. Sometimes the honest first answer is that you don't need an engineer at all, and we'd rather you knew that before you spend anything. If you do need one, <strong>call (08) 5550 6237</strong> and we'll put you in touch.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Perth Hills & Eastern Suburbs</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Perth Hills & Eastern Suburbs Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Wall removal and beam design</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">In a double-brick home some internal walls usually carry the ceiling and roof, and WA builds more brick houses than any other state. Before you open up a kitchen in Midland or Kalamunda, an engineer can check the wall and design the beam.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Crack and structural reports</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">On reactive clay, CSIRO notes that seasonal swelling and shrinkage can make doors bind and cornices crack. An independent engineer's report records what is moving and what is likely driving it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Extensions, second storeys and granny flats</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Footing design depends on the AS 2870 site class, and clay sites are more common in the Perth Hills than on the coastal plain. Your builder or building surveyor will want that engineering settled before the permit goes in.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Patio, carport and shed certificates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A roofed alfresco is not a pergola under the WA exemptions, and a freestanding Colorbond shed over 10 m2 isn't exempt either. The engineer's certificate states the site class and design wind speed the council asks about.</p>
      </div>
</div>
